# Capture payloads are large, binary and machine-specific -- but the NOTES.md
# beside them is the part that makes a capture interpretable six months later,
# so those are tracked. A small, interesting pcap can be force-added as a
# fixture with `git add -f`.
# A global ignore (~/.gitignore_global) excludes `captures/` outright, and an
# excluded *directory* stops git descending into it -- so the directory has to
# be un-ignored first before anything inside can be selectively kept.
!captures/
captures/*
!captures/*/
captures/*/*
!captures/*/NOTES.md
!captures/*/cmd.txt
# captures/journals/ holds the recorder's own timestamped JSONL journals from
# unnamed runs. Never tracked; safe to delete wholesale.
captures/journals/

# Local cache of files pulled off CDJs
cache/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# The generated format matrix: 1 GB of derived audio. tools/make-format-matrix.sh
# rebuilds it, and the source track beside it is what actually matters.
test_tracks/format-matrix/*
!test_tracks/format-matrix/README.md

# The dated capture archive IS committed -- see prolinks-captures-*.7z. It is
# the release asset and the only copy of the pcaps in version control, since
# captures/ itself is ignored.
